title: "Interactive Dashboard of Satellite Imagery and Rainfall for Selected Tropical Cyclones Affecting Puerto Rico (2017–2024)"
abstract: >-
  Interactive dashboard of tropical cyclones affecting Puerto Rico, featuring Irma and
  Maria (2017), Fiona (2022), and Ernesto (2024). NOAA GOES-16 imagery and National
  Hurricane Center tracks are synchronized with a map of accumulated rainfall from
  NWS/NCEP Stage IV, with USGS rain-gauge measurements shown at station locations. The
  archive includes the application, which opens in Spanish and can be switched to
  English, along with the processed data and the scripts used to prepare them.
